  "text": "Iqa‘ Sama‘i Thaqil 10/8 Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Sama‘i Thaqil Iqa‘ Sama‘i Thaqil (also called Sama‘i, for short) is a very popular iqa‘ in the Muwashah vocal genre, as well as the principal iqa‘ used in the Sama‘i Turkish/Ottoman instrumental form. Sama‘i Bayati Ibrahim al-‘Aryan The Takht Ensemble of Cairo Music Of Islam Vol. 1: AL-Qahirah Muwashah ‘Atini Bikra al-Dinan Salim Sahhab Orchestra Muwashah Imlali al-Aqdaha Sirfan Sheikh Hamza Shakkur and Ensemble Al Kindi Muwashah Laha Badru al-Timm Abdel Halim Noueira Ensemble Music by Sheikh Mahmud Subh Muwashah Mala al-Kasat Ensemble Al-Kindi Music by Muhammad ‘Uthman Muwashah Rashiq al-Qadd Ensemble Morkos Cèdre Muwashah Talaffata al-Dhabiyu Ensemble Al-Kindi Music by Sheikh Mahmud Subh Muwashah Tarraza al-Rayhan Ensemble Morkos Cèdre Muwashah Ya Ghusayn al-Ban Sabri al-Mudallal Music by Sayyed Darwish Iqa‘ Sama‘i Thaqil 10/8 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
